+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+The repository does not contain a measured full-recall p95 for the
+`UserPromptSubmit` hook on the adversarial synthetic 30-word vocabulary before
+the term-selection fix. It also does not contain a measured full-recall p95 for
+that exact workload after the fix; those values should not be inferred from the
+other read-path benchmarks.
+
+The fix was to select at most eight prompt terms by inverse document frequency
+(IDF) before issuing the FTS5 BM25 query, dropping terms absent from the store
+and terms whose posting lists are too common to carry useful signal.
+
+For context, the project's recorded stage-level measurement on its 50,000-record
+corpus changed from a p95 of 35.53 ms for BM25 using the first 24 terms to a p95
+of 8.75 ms using the eight highest-IDF terms. These are BM25 stage measurements,
+not the missing end-to-end full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` measurements for the
+adversarial 30-word workload.
